  {
   "id": "sec1-1",
   "section": "History",
   "text": "There are several possible interpretations of Erimena's rise to power.",
   "words": 11,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    11
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1057897866,
   "revisions": [
    1057897866
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    11
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0,
   "footnotes": 0,
   "works_cited": 0,
   "history": {
    "removed": 0,
    "back_within_24h": 0,
    "out_24h_or_more": 0,
    "removing_accounts": 0,
    "restoring_accounts": 0,
    "page_wide_removals": 0,
    "first_added": "2021-11-30",
    "latest_removal": null,
    "in_place_since": "2021-11-30",
    "in_place_since_revision": 1057897866,
    "removals": []
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-2",
   "section": "History",
   "text": "Igor M. Diakonoff believed that Erimena was the brother of Sarduri III and ruled the state due to the fact that, at the time of the death of Sarduri III, his son Sarduri IV had not yet reached adulthood.",
   "words": 39,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    39
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1057897866,
   "revisions": [
    1057897866
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    39
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0,
   "footnotes": 1,
   "works_cited": 1,
   "history": {
    "removed": 0,
    "back_within_24h": 0,
    "out_24h_or_more": 0,
    "removing_accounts": 0,
    "restoring_accounts": 0,
    "page_wide_removals": 0,
    "first_added": "2021-11-30",
    "latest_removal": null,
    "in_place_since": "2021-11-30",
    "in_place_since_revision": 1057897866,
    "removals": []
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-3",
   "section": "History",
   "text": "Erimena is also known from a seal impression of one of his possible governors, preserved on a stone tablet from Karmir-Blur.",
   "words": 22,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    22
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1057897866,
   "revisions": [
    1057897866
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    22
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0,
   "footnotes": 1,
   "works_cited": 1,
   "history": {
    "removed": 0,
    "back_within_24h": 0,
    "out_24h_or_more": 0,
    "removing_accounts": 0,
    "restoring_accounts": 0,
