    "removals": []
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-4",
   "section": "History",
   "text": "In later works, N. V. Harutyunyan, relying on new data from the archaeological excavations at Karmir-Blur, indicated that there are no grounds for such claims and that Erimena simply ascended the throne after Sarduri IV.",
   "words": 36,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    36
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1057897866,
   "revisions": [
    1057897866
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    36
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0,
   "footnotes": 2,
   "works_cited": 2,
   "history": {
    "removed": 0,
    "back_within_24h": 0,
    "out_24h_or_more": 0,
    "removing_accounts": 0,
    "restoring_accounts": 0,
    "page_wide_removals": 0,
    "first_added": "2021-11-30",
    "latest_removal": null,
    "in_place_since": "2021-11-30",
    "in_place_since_revision": 1057897866,
    "removals": []
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-5",
   "section": "History",
   "text": "At the same time, the possibility remains that Erimena was the son of Sarduri IV, and also that Erimena could have been overthrown from the throne by Sarduri IV around 620 BC. and become the founder of a new Urartian dynasty.",
   "words": 41,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    41
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1057897866,
   "revisions": [
    1057897866
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    41
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0,
   "footnotes": 0,
   "works_cited": 0,
   "history": {
    "removed": 0,
    "back_within_24h": 0,
    "out_24h_or_more": 0,
    "removing_accounts": 0,
    "restoring_accounts": 0,
    "page_wide_removals": 0,
    "first_added": "2021-11-30",
    "latest_removal": null,
    "in_place_since": "2021-11-30",
    "in_place_since_revision": 1057897866,
    "removals": []
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-6",
   "section": "History",
   "text": "In addition, there is also a possibility that Sarduri IV was overthrown by Rusa III, the son of Erimena, and Erimena himself was never king (similar to how Sarduri I, the son of Lutipri, ascended the throne after Aram).",
   "words": 39,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    39
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1057897866,
   "revisions": [
    1057897866
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    39
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0,
   "footnotes": 0,
   "works_cited": 0,
   "history": {
    "removed": 0,
    "back_within_24h": 0,
    "out_24h_or_more": 0,
    "removing_accounts": 0,
    "restoring_accounts": 0,
    "page_wide_removals": 0,
    "first_added": "2021-11-30",
