  {
   "id": "sec1-8",
   "section": "History",
   "text": "In the first half of the 20th century, Ivan Meshchaninov suggested that the patronymic of Rusa III does not come from the name of \"Erimena\", but the nationality \"Armenian.”",
   "words": 29,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    29
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1057897866,
